Review of the whole vibestack: sounder checks, more generated, less hand-written

Pipeline: tests and traces are skipped once types or proof fail; spec gen takes
the project lock and shares generation with check; one Node floor; a malformed
package.json is a result, not a crash; check --json streams one line per result;
Result.rules names the rules a result concerns; a proof failure writes a
scaffold with the exact lemma headers; accepted-unproved obligations are
fingerprinted on meaning; the legacy migrate path is gone.

Generator: the persisted Machine layer stored(key) and the React hook
useMachine (gen/<name>.react.ts) replace hand-written copies; partial
operations throw in the Node render; std_ is refused in spec source; one
validator per named type; every supported operator is exercised by a fixture.

Studio: problem, loading, disconnected and empty states; a review dialog that
shows what is signed; failures open their rule; per-stage marks while a check
streams; a change on disk is checked; @repo/ui components in place of
hand-written ones.

Examples: the sender is the by parameter in order and the dashboard tracker;
fullstack's Op is a sum type and its system proof calls the imported units'
lemmas instead of restating them as laws.

The hello-world app exercises one of each feature; design lint and tokens close
their gaps (3:1 control edges); jscpd joins analyze; a tag-triggered release.

